Fix this Normalizer to satisfy the complete business policy. List each correction with its reason, then give all corrected CTL.

The revised manufacturing inspection and recovery export follows this priority schedule, with left-to-right posting order.

1 | planned < 0 or actual < 0 or scrap < 0 or scrap > actual | ERROR {units=0, quality_grade=null, released=false}
2 | quality equals null | HOLD {units=actual, quality_grade=null, released=false}
3 | quality equals "CANCEL" | empty
4 | quality equals "REJECT" and not rework_allowed | SCRAP {units=actual, quality_grade=quality, released=false}
5 | quality equals "REJECT" | GOOD {units=accepted/2, quality_grade=quality, released=true} -> REWORK {units=accepted-accepted/2, quality_grade=quality, released=false} -> SCRAP {units=scrap, quality_grade=quality, released=false}
6 | review | GOOD {units=accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=true} -> AUDIT {units=0, quality_grade=quality, released=false} -> SCRAP {units=scrap, quality_grade=quality, released=false}
7 | accepted+3 < planned | GOOD {units=accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=true} -> SHORT {units=planned-accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=false}
8 | otherwise | GOOD {units=accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=true}

accepted means actual minus scrap. Unit counts are integers; accepted/2 truncates toward zero, and REWORK receives the remainder so GOOD+REWORK+SCRAP equals actual for recoverable rejects. A released flag is true only on GOOD. The supplied inspection grade accompanies each material row except ERROR and missing-inspection HOLD, whose grade is null.

Input 0 Source_manufacturing_1: string batch_id [required]
integer planned [required]
integer actual [required]
integer scrap [required]
string quality [nullability omitted]
boolean rework_allowed [required]
boolean review [required].
Output 0 Posting_manufacturing_1: string source_batch_id [required]
string material_action [required]
integer units [required]
string quality_grade [nullable]
boolean released [required].
Source batch_id values are unique. Preserve each in source_batch_id on its postings.

GOOD and REWORK create distinct recovery versions. SCRAP retains production_version_key rather than creating a recovery. SHORT reports on the last recovery opened by the batch; AUDIT refers to the first one. HOLD and ERROR remain unversioned. Where an annotation refers to an opening, use its version_key; all other unversioned messages use null. A branch producing no postings establishes no versions. The prior identity is supplied on input 0 as production_version_key (long, non-null). It is never replaced on records concerning that prior version.
The destination also carries nullable long version_key and required boolean opens_version, indicating whether that posting establishes a version.
Fresh version numbers come from primitive sequence RecoveryVersionSK, whose first value is 4100002400 and increment is 1; reset it for this run. Every opened version needs its own number, including separate openings from one source event.

Current implementation:
```ctl
//#CTL2
string manufacturing_1_source;
string[] manufacturing_1_material_action_rows = [];
integer[] manufacturing_1_units_rows = [];
string[] manufacturing_1_quality_grade_rows = [];
boolean[] manufacturing_1_released_rows = [];
long[] recovery_version_keys = [];
boolean[] recovery_opens = [];
long recovery_first_open;
long recovery_last_open;
long recovery_prior;
function void stage_manufacturing_1(string p0, integer p1, string p2, boolean p3) {
    append(manufacturing_1_material_action_rows, p0);
    append(manufacturing_1_units_rows, p1);
    append(manufacturing_1_quality_grade_rows, p2);
    append(manufacturing_1_released_rows, p3);
    boolean opening = p0 == "GOOD" || p0 == "REWORK";
    long assigned_key = null;
    if (opening) {
        assigned_key = sequence(RecoveryVersionSK, long).next();
        if (recovery_first_open == null) recovery_first_open = assigned_key;
        recovery_last_open = assigned_key;
    } else if (p0 == "SCRAP") {
        assigned_key = recovery_prior;
    }
    append(recovery_version_keys, assigned_key);
    append(recovery_opens, opening);
}
function void resolve_recovery_links() {
    for (integer k = 0; k < length(manufacturing_1_material_action_rows); k++) {
        if (manufacturing_1_material_action_rows[k] == "AUDIT")
            recovery_version_keys[k] = recovery_first_open != null ? recovery_first_open : recovery_prior;
        else if (manufacturing_1_material_action_rows[k] == "SHORT")
            recovery_version_keys[k] = recovery_last_open != null ? recovery_last_open : recovery_prior;
    }
}
function integer count() {
    recovery_version_keys = [];
    recovery_opens = [];
    recovery_first_open = null;
    recovery_last_open = null;
    recovery_prior = $in.0.production_version_key;
    manufacturing_1_material_action_rows = [];
    manufacturing_1_units_rows = [];
    manufacturing_1_quality_grade_rows = [];
    manufacturing_1_released_rows = [];
    manufacturing_1_source = $in.0.batch_id;
    integer accepted = $in.0.actual-$in.0.scrap;
    /* Branch census:
       1. impossible production -> 1 rows
       2. missing inspection -> 1 rows
       3. batch cancellation -> 0 rows
       4. rejected grade without recovery -> 1 rows
       5. recoverable rejected grade -> 3 rows
       6. reviewed accepted batch -> 3 rows
       7. short production -> 2 rows
       8. ordinary accepted production -> 1 rows
    */
    if ($in.0.planned < 0 || $in.0.actual < 0 || $in.0.scrap < 0 || $in.0.scrap > $in.0.actual) {
        stage_manufacturing_1("ERROR", 0, null, false);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 1; // impossible production
    }
    else if ($in.0.quality == null) {
        stage_manufacturing_1("HOLD", $in.0.actual, null, false);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 1; // missing inspection
    }
    else if ($in.0.quality == "CANCEL") {
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 0; // batch cancellation
    }
    else if ($in.0.quality == "REJECT" && !$in.0.rework_allowed) {
        stage_manufacturing_1("SCRAP", $in.0.actual, $in.0.quality, false);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 1; // rejected grade without recovery
    }
    else if ($in.0.quality == "REJECT") {
        stage_manufacturing_1("GOOD", accepted/2, $in.0.quality, true);
        stage_manufacturing_1("REWORK", accepted-accepted/2, $in.0.quality, false);
        stage_manufacturing_1("SCRAP", $in.0.scrap, $in.0.quality, false);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 3; // recoverable rejected grade
    }
    else if ($in.0.review) {
        stage_manufacturing_1("GOOD", accepted, $in.0.quality, true);
        stage_manufacturing_1("AUDIT", 0, $in.0.quality, false);
        stage_manufacturing_1("SCRAP", $in.0.scrap, $in.0.quality, false);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 3; // reviewed accepted batch
    }
    else if (accepted+3L < $in.0.planned) {
        stage_manufacturing_1("GOOD", accepted, $in.0.quality, true);
        stage_manufacturing_1("SHORT", $in.0.planned-accepted, $in.0.quality, false);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 2; // short production
    }
    else if (true) {
        stage_manufacturing_1("GOOD", accepted, $in.0.quality, true);
        resolve_recovery_links();
        return 1; // ordinary accepted production
    }
    resolve_recovery_links();
    return 0;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    if (recovery_opens[idx]) recovery_version_keys[idx] = sequence(RecoveryVersionSK, long).next();
    $out.0.source_batch_id = manufacturing_1_source;
    $out.0.material_action = manufacturing_1_material_action_rows[idx];
    $out.0.units = manufacturing_1_units_rows[idx];
    $out.0.quality_grade = manufacturing_1_quality_grade_rows[idx];
    $out.0.released = manufacturing_1_released_rows[idx];
    $out.0.version_key = recovery_version_keys[idx];
    $out.0.opens_version = recovery_opens[idx];
    return ALL;
}
```

